apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: dev
  labels:
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted


Privileged Standard  Privileged = "Almost no Pod security restrictions"
--------------------
- Privileged containers: allowed
- Running as root: allowed
- HostNetwork: allowed
- HostPID: allowed
- HostIPC: allowed
- HostPath volumes: allowed
- Linux capabilities: generally unrestricted
- Privilege escalation: allowed
- Seccomp: not required
- AppArmor/SELinux restrictions: not enforced by this standard



Baseline Standard  Baseline = "Block common dangerous Pod settings"
-----------------
- Privileged containers: NOT allowed
- HostNetwork: NOT allowed
- HostPID: NOT allowed
- HostIPC: NOT allowed
- HostPath volumes: NOT allowed
- Dangerous Linux capabilities: restricted
- Host ports: restricted
- AppArmor/SELinux unsafe configurations: restricted
- ProcMount: restricted
- Seccomp: unsafe configurations restricted




Restricted Standard   Restricted = "Strong Pod hardening"
-------------------
Everything from Baseline, plus:

- Container must run as non-root
- runAsNonRoot: required
- Privilege escalation: NOT allowed
- Seccomp profile: required
- Allowed seccomp profiles are restricted
- Linux capabilities: must drop ALL
- Only limited capabilities can be added back
- Host namespaces: NOT allowed
- HostPath: NOT allowed
- Privileged containers: NOT allowed
- Host ports: restricted

PSA MODES

enforce
  Violating Pods are rejected.

audit
  Violations are recorded in audit information.

warn
  User receives a warning.

Important:
enforce/audit/warn = modes
privileged/baseline/restricted = security standards
